      "id": "kbbuz7o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Mineral Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Minerals in India are broadly classified into metallic, non-metallic, and energy resources.",
        "Major metallic minerals include iron ore, manganese, bauxite, and copper distributed across specific geographic belts.",
        "Energy resources comprise conventional fuels such as coal and petroleum alongside non-conventional sources.",
        "India's mineral deposits are concentrated in distinct mineral belts such as the Chota Nagpur Belt.",
        "Conservation of non-renewable mineral resources is crucial for sustainable economic development."
      ],
      "id": "vc2swr9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f71lkyi",
      "content": "• Minerals are natural substances found in rocks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c2osbui",
      "content": "• They are formed through geological processes over millions of years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zfpihos",
      "content": "• Minerals are essential raw materials for industries."
    },
